  'The mandatory foundation for every VTIARA role: values, hygiene, consent, privacy and emergency awareness.', 'Common Core is the shared foundation every VTIARA team member completes before role training. It covers how we present ourselves, how we speak with patients, and the hygiene, infection-control, consent and privacy habits that keep every patient safe. It ends with a 20-question knowledge test and a supervised hand-hygiene practical.', 'Every new and existing VTIARA team member, and future trainees from outside the clinic, regardless of final role.', array['No prior clinical qualification required','Basic reading comprehension in English','Willingness to attend the academy practical session']::text[], array['Explain VTIARA values and uphold grooming and presentation standards','Communicate with patients clearly, kindly and within role scope','Describe skin and hair basics without diagnosing or advising treatment','Perform hand hygiene correctly and apply infection-control precautions','Segregate biomedical waste correctly','Obtain and respect consent, privacy and confidentiality','Respond to fire and medical emergencies by escalating promptly']::text[], array['100% attendance at the academy session','80% or higher on the 20-question knowledge test','Hand-hygiene practical passed']::text[], '{"attendance_pct":100,"knowledge_pct":80,"practical":"Hand-hygiene practical passed"}'::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

